## Monitoring During Execution

When executing multi-task plans, use `/loop` to catch regressions early:

| When | /loop Command | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| After modifying scraping/analysis code | `/loop 5m run pnpm run check:pipeline, report if stuck > 0` | Detect pipeline regressions |
| During multi-file TypeScript changes | `/loop 10m run pnpm run typecheck, report new errors` | Catch type errors early |
| After modifying background jobs | `/loop 5m run pnpm run check:events, report failed jobs` | Detect job failures |
| Long-running implementation sessions | `/loop 30m check node process memory` | Detect memory leaks |

**When NOT to use /loop**:
- Single-file changes (just run verification directly)
- Quick fixes (overhead exceeds value)
- When you're actively writing code (wait until a task boundary)

See the `dev-monitoring` skill for thresholds, remediation actions, and PowerShell patterns.

